{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KSYSocZ1ReoYVQ7UmefKAC","type":"tool_result","content":"460\tpicker, confirm, git panel) is open — so a TUI left sitting in a tmux pane\n461\tcatches up on its own instead of showing a stale job list and jdi badges\n462\tuntil a manual refresh. Its\n463\t\"a\" launch-an-agent picker behaves like the CLI's `mg agents` picker:\n464\t↑/↓/k/j navigate, type to filter (case-insensitive substring over the\n465\tagent's name and description, narrowing the list until esc clears it), enter\n466\tlaunches the highlighted agent, esc clears the filter before cancelling, and\n467\tq cancels. The detail view's `t` key opens the job's branch diff in tig on\n468\tthe host (`mg diff <job> --tig`) in a tmux split pane / new terminal exactly\n469\tlike an agent launch; the footer hint and the key are gated on tig being\n470\tinstalled on the host. The detail view's `l` key tails the job's\n471\t`session.log` live — the verbose raw stream mg-jdi writes each invocation's\n472\toutput into as it happens, a plain `tail -f` of the job's own\n473\t`docs/jobs/<id>_<slug>/session.log` — spawned in a tmux split pane / new\n474\tterminal like an agent launch; the footer hint and the key are gated on a\n475\t`session.log` existing for the job (created at mg-jdi run start). This is\n476\tthe log-vs-tail distinction: the log tab (key 5) reads the sidecar's\n477\t`run.log`, the per-invocation *event summary* (agent invoked / result / next\n478\tagent invoked), while `l` tails the verbose *raw stream*.\n479\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24c1a82b-aecc-49e0-8a6c-9a9931b7cfe5","uuid":"84a8eb83-ba93-4336-a1f8-fc273170b859","timestamp":"2026-08-28T17:50:45.681Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md","content":"picker, confirm, git panel) is open — so a TUI left sitting in a tmux pane\ncatches up on its own instead of showing a stale job list and jdi badges\nuntil a manual refresh. Its\n\"a\" launch-an-agent picker behaves like the CLI's `mg agents` picker:\n↑/↓/k/j navigate, type to filter (case-insensitive substring over the\nagent's name and description, narrowing the list until esc clears it), enter\nlaunches the highlighted agent, esc clears the filter before cancelling, and\nq cancels. The detail view's `t` key opens the job's branch diff in tig on\nthe host (`mg diff <job> --tig`) in a tmux split pane / new terminal exactly\nlike an agent launch; the footer hint and the key are gated on tig being\ninstalled on the host. The detail view's `l` key tails the job's\n`session.log` live — the verbose raw stream mg-jdi writes each invocation's\noutput into as it happens, a plain `tail -f` of the job's own\n`docs/jobs/<id>_<slug>/session.log` — spawned in a tmux split pane / new\nterminal like an agent launch; the footer hint and the key are gated on a\n`session.log` existing for the job (created at mg-jdi run start). This is\nthe log-vs-tail distinction: the log tab (key 5) reads the sidecar's\n`run.log`, the per-invocation *event summary* (agent invoked / result / next\nagent invoked), while `l` tails the verbose *raw stream*.\n","numLines":20,"startLine":460,"totalLines":760}}}
