{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018mvvVHRFi1sALqQy3e1P53","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation: add jq to tailing\n2\t\n3\tid: break\n4\tstatus: open\n5\tdeveloper: @developer\n6\tdate: 2026-08-28\n7\t\n8\t<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n9\t\n10\t## Summary\n11\t\n12\tImplemented the analyst's decision: the TUI's `l` key (`launch.Tail`) now\n13\tpipes the `tail -f` of a job's `session.log` through\n14\t`jq -R -r 'fromjson? // .'` when `jq` is available on the host, pretty-\n15\tprinting the JSONL raw stream both agent CLIs write while passing mg-jdi's\n16\t`=== ... ===` section headers and blank lines through unchanged. When `jq`\n17\tisn't on the host, `Tail` silently falls back to the plain `tail -f` it used\n18\tbefore — no regression for hosts without `jq`. All five task files from\n19\t`tasks.md` were touched; build, vet, and the targeted test suites pass.\n20\t\n21\t## Changes\n22\t\n23\tTASK-1: Added a `JqLookPath`/`JqAvailable` seam to the launch package,\n24\tmirroring the existing `TigLookPath`/`TigAvailable` pattern exactly (an\n25\texported `exec.LookPath`-backed var plus a lightweight availability check),\n26\tpurely additive.\n27\t     files: src/internal/launch/launch.go, src/internal/launch/launch_test.go\n28\t\n29\tTASK-2: Added a parallel `jqTailShellCommand` builder alongside the existing\n30\t`tailShellCommand` (kept unchanged, per the analysis's \"separate function per\n31\tlaunch path\" convention) and made `Tail` pick between them on\n32\t`JqAvailable()`. Neither builder is wrapped in `holdOnFailure` — Ctrl+C\n33\t(exit 130) must still close the pane cleanly on both the plain and piped\n34\tforms.\n35\t     files: src/internal/launch/launch.go, src/internal/launch/launch_test.go\n36\t\n37\tTASK-3: Added `stubJqLookPath` to `internal/ui/tail_test.go` (mirroring\n38\t`stubTigLookPath` in `tig_test.go`) and updated\n39\t`TestTailKeyLaunchesTailInTmuxPane` to stub jq as available so it asserts the\n40\texact jq-piped command deterministically instead of depending on whether the\n41\ttest machine has jq. Added `TestTailKeyFallsBackToPlainTailWhenJqMissing` for\n42\tthe other branch.\n43\t     files: src/internal/ui/tail_test.go\n44\t\n45\tTASK-4: Updated the canonical `docs/AGENTS.md` and\n46\t`project-template/docs/AGENTS.md` descriptions of the `l` tail key to mention\n47\tthe jq pipe and its fallback to plain `tail -f`. Confirmed (grep) that no\n48\t`agents/*.md` file mentions tailing, so none needed a change.\n49\t     files: docs/AGENTS.md, project-template/docs/AGENTS.md\n50\t\n51\tTASK-5: Verified `go build ./...` and `go vet ./...` (both clean), and\n52\t`go test ./internal/launch/... ./internal/ui/... -run 'Jq|Tail'` (all pass).\n53\tA full `go test ./...` was also run: every failure it reports is pre-existing\n54\tand environmental — this session's git shim refuses `git init`\n55\t(\"`git 'init' is not allowed in agent sessions`\"), which many unrelated test\n56\tsuites (internal/git, internal/job, internal/session, cmd/mg, plus the\n57\tnon-tail tests in internal/ui) use to build throwaway fixture repos; none of\n58\tthe failures touch tail/jq code. The manual smoke test from the task\n59\tdescription (`printf '=== ... ===\\n{\"type\":\"message\",\"content\":\"hi\"}\\n\\n' |\n60\tjq -R -r 'fromjson? // .'`) could not be run directly: `jq` is not installed\n61\ton this host and installing packages requires asking first, which is out of\n62\tscope for a non-interactive session — see Known issues below.\n63\t     files: none (verification only)\n64\t\n65\t## Known issues / follow-ups\n66\t\n67\t- The manual jq-pipeline smoke test called for in `tasks.md` TASK-5 was not\n68\t  run against a real `jq` binary — this host has none installed, and\n69\t  installing one needs to be asked about first. The filter's exact\n70\t  construction (`jqTailShellCommand`) is covered by unit tests instead\n71\t  (`TestJqTailShellCommandFormat` and friends), and the filter itself\n72\t  (`jq -R -r 'fromjson? // .'`) is the one specified by the analyst's\n73\t  decision in `tasks.md`. Worth a real-jq smoke test on a host that has it\n74\t  before merging, if that matters to the reviewer.\n75\t- Nothing else found in scope but left undone.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dce4e397-b867-4562-a7a0-8b4087eba22f","uuid":"b94db300-293b-4299-a416-df4d567e96ee","timestamp":"2026-08-28T17:52:18.591Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/break_add-jq-to-tailing/implementation.md","content":"# Implementation: add jq to tailing\n\nid: break\nstatus: open\ndeveloper: @developer\ndate: 2026-08-28\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the analyst's decision: the TUI's `l` key (`launch.Tail`) now\npipes the `tail -f` of a job's `session.log` through\n`jq -R -r 'fromjson? // .'` when `jq` is available on the host, pretty-\nprinting the JSONL raw stream both agent CLIs write while passing mg-jdi's\n`=== ... ===` section headers and blank lines through unchanged. When `jq`\nisn't on the host, `Tail` silently falls back to the plain `tail -f` it used\nbefore — no regression for hosts without `jq`. All five task files from\n`tasks.md` were touched; build, vet, and the targeted test suites pass.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: Added a `JqLookPath`/`JqAvailable` seam to the launch package,\nmirroring the existing `TigLookPath`/`TigAvailable` pattern exactly (an\nexported `exec.LookPath`-backed var plus a lightweight availability check),\npurely additive.\n     files: src/internal/launch/launch.go, src/internal/launch/launch_test.go\n\nTASK-2: Added a parallel `jqTailShellCommand` builder alongside the existing\n`tailShellCommand` (kept unchanged, per the analysis's \"separate function per\nlaunch path\" convention) and made `Tail` pick between them on\n`JqAvailable()`. Neither builder is wrapped in `holdOnFailure` — Ctrl+C\n(exit 130) must still close the pane cleanly on both the plain and piped\nforms.\n     files: src/internal/launch/launch.go, src/internal/launch/launch_test.go\n\nTASK-3: Added `stubJqLookPath` to `internal/ui/tail_test.go` (mirroring\n`stubTigLookPath` in `tig_test.go`) and updated\n`TestTailKeyLaunchesTailInTmuxPane` to stub jq as available so it asserts the\nexact jq-piped command deterministically instead of depending on whether the\ntest machine has jq. Added `TestTailKeyFallsBackToPlainTailWhenJqMissing` for\nthe other branch.\n     files: src/internal/ui/tail_test.go\n\nTASK-4: Updated the canonical `docs/AGENTS.md` and\n`project-template/docs/AGENTS.md` descriptions of the `l` tail key to mention\nthe jq pipe and its fallback to plain `tail -f`. Confirmed (grep) that no\n`agents/*.md` file mentions tailing, so none needed a change.\n     files: docs/AGENTS.md, project-template/docs/AGENTS.md\n\nTASK-5: Verified `go build ./...` and `go vet ./...` (both clean), and\n`go test ./internal/launch/... ./internal/ui/... -run 'Jq|Tail'` (all pass).\nA full `go test ./...` was also run: every failure it reports is pre-existing\nand environmental — this session's git shim refuses `git init`\n(\"`git 'init' is not allowed in agent sessions`\"), which many unrelated test\nsuites (internal/git, internal/job, internal/session, cmd/mg, plus the\nnon-tail tests in internal/ui) use to build throwaway fixture repos; none of\nthe failures touch tail/jq code. The manual smoke test from the task\ndescription (`printf '=== ... ===\\n{\"type\":\"message\",\"content\":\"hi\"}\\n\\n' |\njq -R -r 'fromjson? // .'`) could not be run directly: `jq` is not installed\non this host and installing packages requires asking first, which is out of\nscope for a non-interactive session — see Known issues below.\n     files: none (verification only)\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- The manual jq-pipeline smoke test called for in `tasks.md` TASK-5 was not\n  run against a real `jq` binary — this host has none installed, and\n  installing one needs to be asked about first. The filter's exact\n  construction (`jqTailShellCommand`) is covered by unit tests instead\n  (`TestJqTailShellCommandFormat` and friends), and the filter itself\n  (`jq -R -r 'fromjson? // .'`) is the one specified by the analyst's\n  decision in `tasks.md`. Worth a real-jq smoke test on a host that has it\n  before merging, if that matters to the reviewer.\n- Nothing else found in scope but left undone.\n","numLines":76,"startLine":1,"totalLines":76}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GpJkUcx7Uj7sELcpzZKudJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tasks: add jq to tailing\n2\t\n3\tid: break\n4\tstatus: open\n5\tanalyst: deepseek-v4-flash (read-only analyst)\n6\tdate: 2026-08-28\n7\t\n8\t<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n9\t\n10\t## Analysis summary\n11\t\n12\tThe \"l\" key in the TUI detail view spawns a host-side pane running a plain\n13\t`tail -f '<jobdir>/session.log'` — `launch.Tail` → `tailShellCommand` →\n14\t`launchDetached` (src/internal/launch/launch.go), wired from the \"l\" handler\n15\tin src/internal/ui/app.go, gated on session.log existing (detail.go\n16\t`sessionLogExists`). The pane is a tmux split / new terminal **on the host**,\n17\tso any formatting tool must exist on the host, not in the container.\n18\t\n19\tsession.log is NOT pure JSON: mg-jdi writes `=== <RFC3339> <agent> (attempt\n20\tN) ===` section headers and blank lines around each invocation's raw stream\n21\t(src/cmd/mg/jdioutput.go `openSessionLog`), and the raw stream itself is\n22\tJSONL for BOTH CLIs (opencode `--format json`; Claude `--output-format\n23\tstream-json`). A naive `tail -f x | jq .` would error on the header lines.\n24\t\n25\tDecision (the brief invited an opinion): pipe through jq with the\n26\tmixed-content filter `jq -R -r 'fromjson? // .'` — each line is parsed as\n27\tJSON when possible (pretty-printed, jq's default), and non-JSON lines\n28\t(headers, blanks) fall through raw. jq is soft-gated exactly like tig\n29\t(`launch.TigLookPath`/`TigAvailable`): when jq is missing on the host the\n30\ttail falls back to the plain `tail -f` instead of erroring — strictly better\n31\tthan the status quo. Rejected alternatives: hard-requiring jq (\"readily\n32\tavailable\" ≠ guaranteed, and an error where today there is working behavior\n33\tis a regression), a Go-side formatter subcommand (over-engineering for what a\n34\tone-line pipe does), python3 (not guaranteed on the host).\n35\t\n36\tOut of scope: the serve API's session.log tail (internal/serve/api.go\n37\t`readFileTail` — plain text over HTTP; formatting is the client's concern),\n38\t`mg jdi`'s direct-CLI live terminal stream (different surface, not the \"l\"\n39\tkey), and the TUI log tab (run.log is prose, not JSON). No Dockerfile change\n40\t— the pane is host-side.\n41\t\n42\t## Task breakdown\n43\t\n44\tTASK-1: Add a jq availability seam to the launch package\n45\t     files: src/internal/launch/launch.go, src/internal/launch/launch_test.go\n46\t     depends: none\n47\t     risk: low — mirrors the existing TigLookPath/TigAvailable seam\n48\t     (an exported `JqLookPath = exec.LookPath` var + `JqAvailable()`),\n49\t     purely additive; no behavior change.\n50\t\n51\tTASK-2: Pipe the tail through jq when available\n52\t     files: src/internal/launch/launch.go, src/internal/launch/launch_test.go\n53\t     depends: TASK-1\n54\t     risk: medium — the pane command becomes\n55\t     `tail -f '<path>' | jq -R -r 'fromjson? // .'`: the filter must pass\n56\t     the `=== ... ===` headers and blank lines through raw while\n57\t     pretty-printing JSONL lines, the command string is re-parsed by\n58\t     bash -lc / osascript so quoting must hold, and the deliberate\n59\t     no-holdOnFailure behavior (Ctrl+C exit 130 closes the pane cleanly)\n60\t     must be preserved for both forms. Prefer keeping `tailShellCommand`\n61\t     unchanged and adding a parallel `jqTailShellCommand` builder (the\n62\t     file's separate-function-per-path convention); `Tail` picks on\n63\t     `JqAvailable()`, silently falling back to plain `tail -f` when jq is\n64\t     missing. No TUI code change needed — the launch path owns the decision.\n65\t\n66\tTASK-3: Make the TUI tail tests environment-independent\n67\t     files: src/internal/ui/tail_test.go\n68\t     depends: TASK-2\n69\t     risk: low — stub `launch.JqLookPath` (mirror stubTigLookPath in\n70\t     tig_test.go) so TestTailKeyLaunchesTailInTmuxPane asserts the exact\n71\t     jq-piped command when jq resolves and the plain command when it is\n72\t     missing, instead of depending on whether the test machine has jq.\n73\t\n74\tTASK-4: Update the docs describing the \"l\" tail\n75\t     files: docs/AGENTS.md (canonical, mounted at /workspace/AGENTS.md),\n76\t     project-template/docs/AGENTS.md (mentions the `l` key, lines ~60-66);\n77\t     agents/*.md do NOT mention tailing (verified — no change needed there)\n78\t     depends: TASK-2\n79\t     risk: low — doc-only; \"a plain `tail -f`\" becomes \"a `tail -f` piped\n80\t     through jq when available on the host, falling back to plain tail -f\".\n81\t\n82\tTASK-5: Verify\n83\t     files: none (verification only)\n84\t     depends: TASK-2, TASK-3\n85\t     risk: low — `go build ./...` and `go test ./internal/launch\n86\t     ./internal/ui` (plus the rest of the module as feasible), and a manual\n87\t     smoke of the pipeline against a sample session.log with headers +\n88\t     JSONL: printf '=== 2026-08-28T00:00:00Z analyst (attempt 1)\n89\t     ===\\n{\"type\":\"message\",\"content\":\"hi\"}\\n\\n' | jq -R -r 'fromjson? // .'\n90\t     — headers/blank lines must pass through raw, JSON lines pretty-printed."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dce4e397-b867-4562-a7a0-8b4087eba22f","uuid":"ddc079a1-561f-43da-9c07-b983b1fbbfc1","timestamp":"2026-08-28T17:52:18.592Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/break_add-jq-to-tailing/tasks.md","content":"# Tasks: add jq to tailing\n\nid: break\nstatus: open\nanalyst: deepseek-v4-flash (read-only analyst)\ndate: 2026-08-28\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Analysis summary\n\nThe \"l\" key in the TUI detail view spawns a host-side pane running a plain\n`tail -f '<jobdir>/session.log'` — `launch.Tail` → `tailShellCommand` →\n`launchDetached` (src/internal/launch/launch.go), wired from the \"l\" handler\nin src/internal/ui/app.go, gated on session.log existing (detail.go\n`sessionLogExists`). The pane is a tmux split / new terminal **on the host**,\nso any formatting tool must exist on the host, not in the container.\n\nsession.log is NOT pure JSON: mg-jdi writes `=== <RFC3339> <agent> (attempt\nN) ===` section headers and blank lines around each invocation's raw stream\n(src/cmd/mg/jdioutput.go `openSessionLog`), and the raw stream itself is\nJSONL for BOTH CLIs (opencode `--format json`; Claude `--output-format\nstream-json`). A naive `tail -f x | jq .` would error on the header lines.\n\nDecision (the brief invited an opinion): pipe through jq with the\nmixed-content filter `jq -R -r 'fromjson? // .'` — each line is parsed as\nJSON when possible (pretty-printed, jq's default), and non-JSON lines\n(headers, blanks) fall through raw. jq is soft-gated exactly like tig\n(`launch.TigLookPath`/`TigAvailable`): when jq is missing on the host the\ntail falls back to the plain `tail -f` instead of erroring — strictly better\nthan the status quo. Rejected alternatives: hard-requiring jq (\"readily\navailable\" ≠ guaranteed, and an error where today there is working behavior\nis a regression), a Go-side formatter subcommand (over-engineering for what a\none-line pipe does), python3 (not guaranteed on the host).\n\nOut of scope: the serve API's session.log tail (internal/serve/api.go\n`readFileTail` — plain text over HTTP; formatting is the client's concern),\n`mg jdi`'s direct-CLI live terminal stream (different surface, not the \"l\"\nkey), and the TUI log tab (run.log is prose, not JSON). No Dockerfile change\n— the pane is host-side.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Add a jq availability seam to the launch package\n     files: src/internal/launch/launch.go, src/internal/launch/launch_test.go\n     depends: none\n     risk: low — mirrors the existing TigLookPath/TigAvailable seam\n     (an exported `JqLookPath = exec.LookPath` var + `JqAvailable()`),\n     purely additive; no behavior change.\n\nTASK-2: Pipe the tail through jq when available\n     files: src/internal/launch/launch.go, src/internal/launch/launch_test.go\n     depends: TASK-1\n     risk: medium — the pane command becomes\n     `tail -f '<path>' | jq -R -r 'fromjson? // .'`: the filter must pass\n     the `=== ... ===` headers and blank lines through raw while\n     pretty-printing JSONL lines, the command string is re-parsed by\n     bash -lc / osascript so quoting must hold, and the deliberate\n     no-holdOnFailure behavior (Ctrl+C exit 130 closes the pane cleanly)\n     must be preserved for both forms. Prefer keeping `tailShellCommand`\n     unchanged and adding a parallel `jqTailShellCommand` builder (the\n     file's separate-function-per-path convention); `Tail` picks on\n     `JqAvailable()`, silently falling back to plain `tail -f` when jq is\n     missing. No TUI code change needed — the launch path owns the decision.\n\nTASK-3: Make the TUI tail tests environment-independent\n     files: src/internal/ui/tail_test.go\n     depends: TASK-2\n     risk: low — stub `launch.JqLookPath` (mirror stubTigLookPath in\n     tig_test.go) so TestTailKeyLaunchesTailInTmuxPane asserts the exact\n     jq-piped command when jq resolves and the plain command when it is\n     missing, instead of depending on whether the test machine has jq.\n\nTASK-4: Update the docs describing the \"l\" tail\n     files: docs/AGENTS.md (canonical, mounted at /workspace/AGENTS.md),\n     project-template/docs/AGENTS.md (mentions the `l` key, lines ~60-66);\n     agents/*.md do NOT mention tailing (verified — no change needed there)\n     depends: TASK-2\n     risk: low — doc-only; \"a plain `tail -f`\" becomes \"a `tail -f` piped\n     through jq when available on the host, falling back to plain tail -f\".\n\nTASK-5: Verify\n     files: none (verification only)\n     depends: TASK-2, TASK-3\n     risk: low — `go build ./...` and `go test ./internal/launch\n     ./internal/ui` (plus the rest of the module as feasible), and a manual\n     smoke of the pipeline against a sample session.log with headers +\n     JSONL: printf '=== 2026-08-28T00:00:00Z analyst (attempt 1)\n     ===\\n{\"type\":\"message\",\"content\":\"hi\"}\\n\\n' | jq -R -r 'fromjson? // .'\n     — headers/blank lines must pass through raw, JSON lines pretty-printed.","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}}}
