{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DBCozmD216H1wKhR31KpTE","type":"tool_result","content":"95\tfinished, here's what needs a human\" — surfaced through the notification\n96\tchannel already built. The old \"attended terminal\" objection is mostly\n97\tobsoleted by the machinery built since.\n98\t\n99\t### 5. Event-streaming subsystem — designed against a real consumer, now in scope\n100\t\n101\t**Status: PARTIALLY addressed** — the writer side landed in\n102\t`health_capture-non-interactive-agent-sessions`: every non-interactive\n103\tinvocation's raw step-level output is now streamed *live* into the job's own\n104\t`session.log` during the run (and claude-pro's `--print` path emits the full\n105\tstream-json event stream), superseding the README's honest \"final answer\n106\tonly\" limitation. The reader side has partly landed in\n107\t`guest_fix-tailing`: the detail view's `l` key now tails `session.log` — a\n108\t`tail -f` pane of the verbose raw stream, distinct from the log tab's\n109\t`run.log` event summary. What remains open is the item's richer *in-TUI*\n110\tstep-level view — the TUI log tab stays on `run.log` for now; rendering\n111\t`session.log` as a structured step-level view inside the TUI is a separate,\n112\tlater job (the `l` tail pane is the interim reader).\n113\t\n114\tThe polling model tells you the *stage*, not what the agent is *doing*. The"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dce4e397-b867-4562-a7a0-8b4087eba22f","uuid":"7bcb9237-e127-44be-b337-d959ffd69100","timestamp":"2026-08-28T17:52:48.723Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/ROADMAP.md","content":"finished, here's what needs a human\" — surfaced through the notification\nchannel already built. The old \"attended terminal\" objection is mostly\nobsoleted by the machinery built since.\n\n### 5. Event-streaming subsystem — designed against a real consumer, now in scope\n\n**Status: PARTIALLY addressed** — the